  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "The third-order initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{\u2034}-6\\sqrt{t}\\,{y}^{\u2033}+12{y}^{\u2032}=0,\\,y(1)=-2,\\,{y}^{\u2032}(1)=2,\\,{y}^{\u2033}(1)=-3\n$$\n\ncan be written as a system of first-order differential equations, as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{\u2032}={x}_{2},\\, & {x}_{1}(1)=p \\\\ {x}_{2}^{\u2032}={x}_{3},\\, & {x}_{2}(1)=q \\\\ {x}_{3}^{\u2032}=f(t),\\, & {x}_{3}(1)=r\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{1}(t)=y(t),$ ${x}_{2}(t)={y}^{\u2032}(t),$ ${x}_{3}(t)={y}^{\u2033}(t),$ and $p,$ $q$ and $r$ are constants. Calculate  $(p+q-r)\\cdot f(t).$",
